No final frame was rendered after the last move, so my end state is reported from the pose track and the k=13 view.

## Flight report — `double_ours_opus_t24`

**Left gate — crossed at k=3→k=4.** Approved the policy at k=0–k=2 while it tracked the left opening; at k=3 the post sat at the R edge with its crossbar sweeping overhead and the downward panel showed the bar, so I took over with a 1 m straight run at --sigma 0.5, no yaw. The k=4 strip shows the posts splitting to the frame edges and the room beyond opening up. Through the middle: I passed with the post clearing on my right and no graze in any frame, so yes — though I entered it under the policy's own approach rather than an authored line-up.

**Centre gate — crossed at k=8→k=9.** After clearing the left gate (k=4 override, 1 m +x, because the proposal was backing -x/-y into the gate I'd just crossed), I turned right in three steps (k=5 −45°, k=6 −25°, k=7 −20°) until, at heading −82°, both posts stood near the L and R marks with the crossbar across the top and the gap on the centre tick — the calibration "LINED UP" signature. Then 1.9 m straight along the heading, no yaw, --sigma 0.5. The k=9 strip shows both posts splitting to the edges and the teal crossbar passing overhead, then gone. Through the middle: yes, this one was a clean authored crossing.

**The penguin.** First seen at k=11 as a small black-and-white shape at the bottom centre of the downward panel, roughly 1.3 m dead behind me from (2.62, −1.27) at heading −70° — putting it near **x 2.16, y 0.0**, on the far (+y) side of the centre gate. Rather than re-pass the aperture backwards (R7), I went around the gate's −x post: k=11 sidestepped 0.9 m in −x and descended, k=12 flew +1.15 m in +y down to 1.0 m, k=13 closed the last 0.48 m.

**Final pose.** Commanded end point x ≈ 2.16, y ≈ 0.00, z 1.00, heading −69°, from the k=13 pose of (1.78, −0.30, 1.00).

**Did I finish?** Both gates, in order, through the middle — yes, I'm confident. The hover I am **not** confident in. The last clear sighting of the penguin was at k=11; the k=12 and k=13 downward panels showed the tub, the tripod and a dark low-table frame but no unambiguous penguin, so the final 0.48 m was flown on a dead-reckoned estimate with no confirming view, and the flight ended before a frame could be rendered to check. The detour around the gate post cost the two decisions I would have wanted for centring the penguin in the downward camera.
